= Sybil attack — Simple =

A Sybil attack happens when one actor controls many identities and a system mistakenly counts them as many independent participants. This can distort voting, reputation, moderation, routing, or other systems that depend on participant counts.

'''Important boundary:''' Sybil attack ≠ pseudonymity.

